Z||000000||fiero651||03-28-2001||12:47 AM||||I have had this car since 92 it is a 86 SE 2M6 notchback with C&C T-Tops put on from the factory.  The reason I am asking is because I can't get any info on it as far as numbers made other than I thought T-tops weren't around until 88.  I am contemplating turning it into a fastback.  But if the combination is extremely rare I won't.  Let me know what you all think.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Kelvin Vivian||03-28-2001||01:27 AM||||From the list below, you have 1 of 28,274 1986 Fiero 2M6 SEs.<P>But, with a T-top, I'm sure that you have one of a very few.<P>T-tops were not a "factory" option until 1988. However, the same company that installed the T-top in your car as an "aftermarket" addition is the same company that installed the "factory" T-top option in 1988, C&C.<P>My vote would be for you to keep it as-is and take it to some Fiero shows!<P>------------------------------<BR>84 Indy Pace Car: 2,000<BR>84 Base Coupe: 7,099<BR>84 Sport Coupe: 62,070<BR>84 SE: 65,671<BR>Total 84 Production: 136,843<P>85 Base Coupe: 5,280<BR>85 Sport Coupe: 23,823<BR>85 SE 4-cyl: 12,901<BR>85 SE V6: 11,833<BR>85 GT: 22,534<BR>Total 85 Production: 76,371<P>86 Base Coupe: 9,143<BR>86 Sport Coupe: 24,866<BR>86 SE 4-cyl: 4,031<BR>86 SE V6: 28,274<BR>86 GT: 17,655<BR>Total 86 Production: 83,969<P>87 Base Coupe: 23,603<BR>87 Sport Coupe: 3,135<BR>87 SE 4-cyl: 1,401<BR>87 SE V6: 2,474<BR>87 GT: 15,966<BR>Total 87 Production: 46,579<P>88 Coupe: 13,910<BR>88 Formula: 5,684<BR>88 GT: 6,849<BR>Total 88 Production: 24,601<P>Options:<BR>T-tops: 1,252 (88 option) (91 coupe + 547 Formula + 614 GT)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||03-28-2001||01:29 AM||||Well its my understanding that you were able to bring your Fiero to C&C to have T-Tops installed. But the only Pontiac Factory T-Top available was in 1988. I'm not sure about it being rare but, The T-Top Fieros are sure saute after. Your not going to be able to find out how many 86 SE's that C&C converted. <P>P.S. Welcome to the Forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">     </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||14
Z||000003||AusFiero||03-28-2001||07:24 AM||||From study I have done around various sources, there was approximately 2500 t-top sets produced by C&C for Fieros.<P>Take off the figures from the known 88 factory option cars (probably available at the t-top registry) and the leftover is a very rough estimate of how many got fitted between 86 and 88 excluding the few sets that was left over and sold off to another supplier.<P>I have an 86 GT fastback with t-tops. I purchased it off the original lady owner who moved from Canada to Australia with Fiero in tow. Those particular t-tops was fitted by a Canadian fitter.<P>Anybody else know of any Canadian 86 GT's with t-tops and a factory KM Hr speedometer? Just trying to see how rare it is.<P>Don't quote me on those figures but the sources they came from are pretty reliable.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CanadianGT||03-28-2001||03:18 PM||||I am here in Canada and I have an 86 GT.  The only difference is my Factory T-tops have still not been installed yet.  They are brand new in there box still, sitting in my basement.  I just recently purchased them off a guy who had them since 1988, but never installed them on his 88 Gt since it was a show car, and he wanted to keep it stock.  I got a really good deal on them for being brand new, and all the pieces are still wrapped in plastic.  I Have not installed them yet, since I am only 18, and dont have enough money to get anyone to install them, and I cant find anyone to do it.  Plus I want to install them on 87 5 speed GT if I ever get one, rather then my automatic.||||reg||1
